`]})}),e.jsxs(n,{title:"The batch factor cancels most of the length factor",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Delphi's learning rate for its projection layers is a product of three factors ",e.jsx(i,{id:"held2026delphi",children:"Held, 2026"}),". The base rate ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"η₀ = 0.0063"})," was tuned on a reference model of about 130M parameters, with batches of ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"B₀ = 64"})," sequences and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"D₀ = 2.5B"})," training tokens. For a run of ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"D"})," tokens with batches of ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"B"})," sequences, the batch factor ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"√(B/B₀)"})," is Week 5's square-root heuristic, and the length factor is ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(D₀/D)^0.3"}),". Embeddings and scalar parameters take a separate Adam rate, which does fall with the token count."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Delphi's largest held-out run, at 1e23 FLOPs, trained a 25B model ",e.jsx(i,{id:"held2026delphi",children:"Held, 2026"}),". By our arithmetic from its steps and batch, it saw 628B tokens, about 250 times the reference's, so the length factor alone would cut the rate to about a fifth, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(2.5/628.2)^0.3 ≈ 0.19"}),", as the widget's held-at-64 view shows. Its batch, 2,048 sequences, was set to fit its hardware ",e.jsx(i,{id:"marin2026delphicode",children:"Marin Community, 2026a"}),". That is 32 times the reference batch, and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"√32 ≈ 5.7"})," cancels most of the length factor, so the rate moves from 0.0063 to 0.0068 (our arithmetic)."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["μP's table has a ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"1/width"})," factor, and the recipe has none. In the post's account, Delphi's optimizer, AdamH, transfers the learning rate across width well enough that the recipe needs no width term ",e.jsx(i,{id:"held2026delphi",children:"Held, 2026"}),". The recipe also scales Adam's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"β₂"})," with the batch, and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ε"})," with the batch and the token count. The widget lists both."]})]})]})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(d,{tab:"Fitted Laws",plate:"manesson-compas-de-proportion",children:[e.jsxs(s,{title:"DeepSeek fits the optimum against compute",accent:0,number:"9",children:[e.jsx(h,{math:"\\eta_{\\mathrm{opt}} = 0.3118\\,C^{-0.125} \\qquad B_{\\mathrm{opt}} = 0.2920\\,C^{0.3271}",label:"DeepSeek fitted hyperparameter laws"}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
